      "updated_at": "2025-12-12T18:53:19Z",
      "body": "The divergence appears to be caused by a different floating-point rounding order. In a single backward step, we observe that the gradient of the output of token_permutation (including the collective communication) is identical across dispatchers, but the gradient of the input differs. This suggests the mismatch is introduced inside token_permutation during the backward path due to a different accumulation / reduction order.",
